  "section_notes": "The final rules set a 24-hour incident reporting deadline and a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which hits Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S2 keeps the 5% limit but only permits the regulator to restrict sales, so Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2% is not forced off the market. S3's 6-year retrofit window also favours Northwind's low 38% shut-off coverage. The S2 customer-results wording ('applicable results') does not specify numeric rates, so the numeric_rates coding is an interpretation."
